# ---- Numbers -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hungarian writes numbers under 2000 as one word: 21-99 compose as "{tens}{units}" ("harminchárom"),
# 101-999 as "{hundreds}{rest}" ("százhuszonöt"). 11-19 ("tizen-") and 21-29 ("huszon-") are listed, as is
# every hundred ("kétszáz", not "kettőszáz").
# Two words for 2: "kettő" alone (a rank: "e kettő", a decimal: "kettő egész öt") and "két" before a noun. The
# form "attr" ({n:attr}, number.<n>.attr.spoken) says "két", "tizenkét", "huszonkét", "harminckét"...;
# every counted noun below uses it, and a line that puts a bare number before a noun must too.
