# ---- Counted nouns ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hungarian plural rule (assets/i18n): one (1) | other. After a number the noun stays singular ("3 hiba"),
# so both forms are the same words (count.time aside). Written: digits ("3 lépés"); spoken: the number
# before a noun in the form "attr" ("két lépés").
# The case suffix goes on the noun: count.<noun>_<case> for every noun below and every case of the
# pieces (acc dat ins sub sup del ill ine ela all ade abl ter cau): {pts:point_acc} = "3 pontot",
# {m:move_ine} = "2 lépésben" (mate in 2), {n:move_ter} = "10 lépésig", {n2:piece_ins} = "2 bábuval".
# A few nouns also have "_nyi", an amount (move_nyi, point_nyi, pawn_nyi, square_nyi: {pts:point_nyi}
# anyag = "3 pontnyi anyag", {n:pawn_nyi} előny = "1 gyalognyi előny"), and "_adj", an adjective (move_adj,
# point_adj, game_adj, percent_adj: {m:move_adj} matt = "3 lépéses matt", {pts:point_adj} előny = "2 pontos
# előny"). count.time has no case forms.
